  "textEn": "There are avenues and ways as broad as blue skies, Yet I find myself confined.\nI feel ashamed and unwilling to gather with aristocratic youths, Who place bets and gamble on red roosters and white hounds with crop yields.\nI'd strike my sword singing my grievances like Guo Huan of history, A life relying on noblemen's hospitality clashes with my will.\nI have not forgotten how General Han Xin was insulted by street philistines, Nor the Han courtiers' jealousy towards the talented Jia Yi.\nDo you not see How Lord Zhao of Yan honoured Guo Wei, Putting aside his status to pay respect to the talented.\nTo this very lord Ju Xin and Yue Yi owed gratitude, And thus to His Lordship they their utmost loyalty sincerely pledged.\nThe remains of Lord Zhao had long been buried among rotten weeds, Who is there now to the celebrated Golden Terrace sweep and maintain?\nOn such a trying journey, perhaps homeward is the way!"
