 "tang300-yuefu|行路難三首 三 · 李白 ②": {
  "year": 2011,
  "url": "https://28utscprojects.wordpress.com/2011/01/11/084/",
  "textEn": "There is no need to cleanse ears with the waters of River Ying, Nor is it necessary to feed on ferns of the Shouyang Mountains.\nBeing unheard of aids the seclusion of virtues of a virtuoso from the worldly, Why focus on portraying one's aloofness in comparison to the sky-high moon and clouds?\nMy observations of the gifted and the heroic suggest Misfortune and death befell those who failed to retreat from public eyes in their success.\nZixu took his own life and the Lord of Wu had his body tossed into River Wu, Qu Yuan threw himself into River Xiang where his patriotic heart perished.\nLu Ji had a great mind but could he his own fate divine? Li Si could only regret why he had not sooner retired.\nIs it any wonder that Lu never visited again the Florid Pavilion to listen to wild geese cry? It goes without saying that Li never went to hunt with his eagle over the Gate of Shangcai. Do you not see Zhang Han of the Wu region was the one who is really liberal and liberated, He'd turn and head for the river's east as an autumn wind suddenly recall home to mind.\nSaying as he left, life should be enjoyed in the moment with a chalice of wine, What of a good reputation and long-lasting fame beyond one's time?"
 },
 "tang300-yuefu|長干曲四首 一 · 崔顥 ②": {
  "year": 2010,
  "url": "https://28utscprojects.wordpress.com/2010/12/12/253/",
  "textEn": "Where is your family home, sir, As for me, I live by the Wide Bay.\nI stop my boat briefly to an enquiry make, I have a feeling we're from the same place."
 },
 "tang300-yuefu|長干曲四首 二 · 崔顥 ②": {
  "year": 2010,
  "url": "https://28utscprojects.wordpress.com/2010/12/12/254/",
  "textEn": "I used to live by the waters of Nine-river Town, I used to go about the nearby waterways.\nThough we're both people of the Changgan region, I left when we were too young to each other's acquaintance make."
 },
 "tang300-yuefu|長干行二首 一 · 李白": {
  "year": 2011,
  "url": "https://28utscprojects.wordpress.com/2011/01/20/043/",
  "textEn": "I had only started to wear my hair banged, Playing around I was picking flowers in the yard at the front;\nYou came around on your bamboo horse Encircling chairs and benches and dangling in your hand was a branch of green plums.\nWe both lived in the region of Changgan, Two youngsters who hadn't thought much.\nAt the age of fourteen I became your wife, Diffident and shy, low I held my head;\nI would retreat to a corner in the shadow, And would not answer to your call after call.\nAt fifteen my brows started to ease, And fell for you till death do us part;\nYou vowed to keep your promises to me, So why would I find myself on the lookout for your homecoming?\nYet when I was sixteen you had to leave home to travel far Through the Yangtze Gorges passing the Yanyu river rock,\nWhich in May would give rise to formidable rugged waters, Gibbons' howling would come from precipices on both sides and resonate skywards.\nThe hesitated footprints from the day you left Have already become moss-covered and green.\nThe moss has grown so thick that sweeping could not do away, Till autumn comes early and leaves fall to the moss conceal.\nAugust sees butterflies turn yellow and frail, And in pairs they'd fly over the west chamber garden, over grass blades.\nSuch a scene saddens me, As I sit in sorrow and wait my youth away.\nOne day whether soon or late on your return through the towns of Ba, Do write a letter home beforehand;\nI care not how far I'd have to travel to receive you on your way, Even if I have to go all the way to Changfengsha."
 },
 "tang300-yuefu|獨不見 · 沈佺期": {
  "year": 2010,
  "url": "https://28utscprojects.wordpress.com/2010/12/17/223/",
  "textEn": "A young woman of a blooming tulip's beauty was married to a Lu family, Her wedded bliss was once as envied as tortoiseshell beams carved with swallows in pairs.\nSeptember's winter garment pressing sounds hurried leaves yellow and trees bare, For ten years her husband had been at the Liaoyang front line to their country defend.\nMessages from north of the White Wolf River were severed, Autumn night south of the Red Phoenix City seemed so long extended.\nEver out of sight was the fountainhead of her ever deepening melancholy and despair, Who couldn't be there to this moment share as the moon shined on her aureate silk dress."
 },
 "tang300-yuefu|秋夜曲 · 王涯 ②": {
  "year": 2010,
  "url": "https://28utscprojects.wordpress.com/2010/11/23/313/",
  "textEn": "The moon has just shown her face on a night with slight autumn dew, Her thin robe is becoming light, yet for a change of clothes she makes no move.\nOn her silver cittern she plays heartily all evening, Concealing her dread of returning to her lonely room."
 },
 "tang300-yuefu|涼州詞二首 一 · 王之渙": {
  "year": 2010,
  "url": "https://28utscprojects.wordpress.com/2010/11/23/316/",
  "textEn": "The Yellow River into the clouds winds and undulates, One lone township lies among towering mountain ranges.\nWhy play the lamenting Willow Ballad on your Jiang flutes, When you know the Gate of Jade spring and barrenness separates."
 }
